### API Testing File
# This file can be used with the "HTTP Client" plugin in Android Studio / IntelliJ.
# It is pre-configured with the custom headers used in the project's network layer.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
@refreshToken = YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN
@devicePlatform = android
@appVersion = 1.0.0
@appVersionCode = 1
@deviceId = your_unique_device_id

### Check User (Login Flow Start)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/check-user
Content-Type: application/json
User-Device: {{deviceId}}hrm
User-Device-Platform: {{devicePlatform}}
User-Device-App-Version: {{appVersion}}
User-Device-App-Version-Code: {{appVersionCode}}

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}

### Verify OTP (Complete Login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json
User-Device: {{deviceId}}hrm
User-Device-Platform: {{devicePlatform}}
User-Device-App-Version: {{appVersion}}
User-Device-App-Version-Code: {{appVersionCode}}

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### Refresh Token
# Used by Ktor's Auth bearer plugin to refresh expired access tokens.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/refresh
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
User-Device: {{deviceId}}hrm
User-Device-Platform: {{devicePlatform}}
User-Device-App-Version: {{appVersion}}

refresh_token={{refreshToken}}

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
User-Device: {{deviceId}}hrm
User-Device-Platform: {{devicePlatform}}

### Refresh User Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/refresh-user-details
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
User-Device: {{deviceId}}hrm
User-Device-Platform: {{devicePlatform}}
User-Device-App-Version: {{appVersion}}
